# CITATION.cff - Citation File Format specification: https://citationcff.code
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HoverBlade-FM in research or industry work, please cite this
  software and the papers listed in docs/literature_review.md."
title: "HoverBlade-FM: hover-only rotor end-to-end generator with a blunt
  trailing-edge hard constraint and Figure-of-Merit maximisation"
abstract: "Given target thrust, rotor radius and minimum trailing-edge thickness,
  HoverBlade-FM resolves the remaining design parameters, generates ten radial
  sections parameterised with a class-shape-transformation (CST) mapping that carries
  an explicit, hard-clamped trailing-edge gap, evaluates hover performance with a
  blade-element-momentum solver using Prandtl tip and root losses plus an analytic
  polar with Reynolds, Mach and blunt-edge drag corrections, maximises the hover
  figure of merit with CMA-ES and an SLSQP refinement, and exports CSV/JSON data,
  plots, an HTML report, an interactive blade view and STEP/STL/DXF manufacturing
  files with a manufacturing report."
authors:
  - name: "HoverBlade-FM contributors"
    entity: true
repository-code: "https://github.com/hoverblade-fm/HoverBlade-FM"
url: "https://github.com/hoverblade-fm/HoverBlade-FM"
license: Apache-2.0
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-14"
keywords:
  - rotor
  - hover
  - figure of merit
  - blade element momentum theory
  - CST
  - airfoil parameterization
  - blunt trailing edge
  - CMA-ES
  - shape optimization
  - manufacturing geometry
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.REPLACE_AT_RELEASE"
    description: "Reserved at the time of writing; the release workflow (T100) fills
      this in once the Zenodo concept DOI exists.  Until then cite the repository URL
      and the commit hash recorded in provenance.json."
references:
  - type: software
    title: "cma: Evolution Strategy Optimization"
    authors:
      - given-names: Nikolaus
        family-names: Hansen
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/1604.00772"
    year: 2016
    notes: "The CMA-ES implementation used for the global search stage."
  - type: software
    title: "SciPy 1.0: fundamental algorithms for scientific computing in Python"
    authors:
      - given-names: Pauli
        family-names: Virtanen
    url: "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41592-019-0686-2"
    year: 2020
    notes: "Provides SLSQP, used for the local refinement stage."
